   = note: a dash between two clauses leaves their relationship for the reader to work out, and marks a sentence carrying more than one thought
   = help: restructure the sentence so each clause carries one thought, rather than putting a different mark where the dash was: make it two sentences, or use the mark that states the relationship (a colon for an elaboration, a semicolon for parallel statements, a comma for a dependent clause)
   = note: `#[warn(perfectionist::em_dash_prose)]` on by default

